@* The framework's web on the Architecture page: the four libraries every site is built on. *@
<Band Id="web" Kicker="src/web · the framework's web">
    <h3>What every site shares.</h3>
    <p class="lede">A site is a small Blazor WebAssembly app on the framework's web: it brings its words, its brand, its pages and the packs' screens it uses, and the rest is here. This site is one.</p>
    <ul class="rules">
        <li><strong><code>louis-agent.web</code></strong> The chat's and the admin's frames, the site frame this page sits in, the chat widget in the corner, the described screens, the API client, markdown, usage and currency.</li>
        <li><strong><code>louis-agent.web.accounts</code></strong> The account pages, their client, words, styles and passkey script. A site with accounts opts in.</li>
        <li><strong><code>louis-agent.web.evals</code></strong> The eval studio's pages: the evals, a run, the review queue, the studio and the prompts.</li>
        <li><strong><code>louis-agent.diagrams</code></strong> The diagrams, drawn from data in plain C#: the boxes and arrows on these pages, and the pictures in the framework's docs.</li>
    </ul>
</Band>
